      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand what's there before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — splitting the single monolithic test into focused methods with descriptive names, and removing unused imports.Now I'll compile-check the test.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored test splits the original single monolithic method into five focused, descriptively named test methods (`decimalDigitsAreValidHexDigits`, `lowercaseHexLettersAreValidHexDigits`, `uppercaseHexLettersAreValidHexDigits`, `nonHexAsciiLettersAreRejected`, `nonAsciiCharactersAreRejected`), removes unused imports, and adds brief comments to clarify the non-obvious Unicode characters — all while calling the same methods with identical arguments and expected outcomes."
    }
